<reference id="_Toc235450412" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 6 — List inside a table cell</title>
   <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>inside</keyword>
        <keyword>table</keyword>
        <keyword>List</keyword>
        <keyword>DITA</keyword>
        <keyword>Scenario</keyword>
        <keyword>cells</keyword>
        <indexterm>inside</indexterm>
        <indexterm>table</indexterm>
        <indexterm>List</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section id="sec_d761e7">
         <p>Consider a table where the author has placed a <codeph>&lt;ul&gt;</codeph> or <codeph>&lt;ol&gt;</codeph> list inside one of the <codeph>&lt;td&gt;</codeph> cells.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>List inside a table cell</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_xx4_lyn_lkc">
&lt;table>
  &lt;tr>
    &lt;th>Step&lt;/th>
    &lt;th>Actions&lt;/th>
  &lt;/tr>
  &lt;tr>
    &lt;td>1&lt;/td>
    &lt;td>
      &lt;ul>
        &lt;li>Download the package.&lt;/li>
        &lt;li>Verify the checksum.&lt;/li>
        &lt;li>Extract the archive.&lt;/li>
      &lt;/ul>
    &lt;/td>
  &lt;/tr>
&lt;/table></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                    
                     
                     
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_brw_lyn_lkc">
&lt;simpletable>
  &lt;sthead>
    &lt;stentry>Step&lt;/stentry>
    &lt;stentry>Actions&lt;/stentry>
  &lt;/sthead>
  &lt;strow>
    &lt;stentry>1&lt;/stentry>
    &lt;stentry>
      &lt;ul>
        &lt;li>Download the package.&lt;/li>
        &lt;li>Verify the checksum.&lt;/li>
        &lt;li>Extract the archive.&lt;/li>
      &lt;/ul>
    &lt;/stentry>
  &lt;/strow>
&lt;/simpletable></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
         <p>
            <b>Result:</b> The converter preserves the <codeph>&lt;ul&gt;</codeph> or <codeph>&lt;ol&gt;</codeph> list inside the table cell and maps it to the corresponding DITA <codeph>&lt;ul&gt;</codeph> or <codeph>&lt;ol&gt;</codeph> element inside <codeph>&lt;stentry&gt;</codeph>.</p>
         <note type="tip"> Use lists inside table cells only when the list represents multiple
            related values for the same row. Avoid using lists inside tables for procedural steps.
            If the content is procedural, consider converting it to a DITA task with
               <codeph>&lt;steps&gt;</codeph>.</note>
      </section>
   </refbody>
